ames-Theorem-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":22,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"0583b6de91971e91e0d0476a3851e097dde30752833576c52eadfc934a117da5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Unique-Games-Theorem-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:129965d2c20bcb2271e1ccb15a95dd8152f29375ec7628f2c71940568e0c2576","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Unique-Games-Theorem-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L22"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:ugc}\nFor every fixed \\(\\varepsilon,\\delta\\in(0,1/2)\\), there are an integer\n\\(s\\ge1\\) and a deterministic polynomial-time reduction from\n\\(\\mathrm{3SAT}\\) to explicit unweighted Unique Games instances\n\\(G_\\varphi\\) over \\(K=\\F_2^s\\) such that\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n \\varphi\\text{ satisfiable}\n &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\val(G_\\varphi)\\ge1-\\varepsilon,\\\\\n \\varphi\\text{ unsatisfiable}\n &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\val(G_\\varphi)\\le\\delta.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe graph is simple and bipartite, and every constraint is a translation\n\\(a(v_e)=a(u_e)+c_e\\) of \\(K\\). The alphabet, the degree of the\nrunning-time polynomial, and its constants depend only on\n\\(\\varepsilon,\\delta\\)."}
